## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical amortized analysis under streaming appends with cache considerations. It evaluates understanding of how to design data structures that balance update frequency, query latency, and memory access patterns.

## Key Concepts
- **Sliding windows**: Maintaining a fixed-size view over streaming data
- **Circular buffers**: O(1) rotation without shifting elements
- **Amortized analysis**: Batched updates spread costs over time
- **Cache-friendly layout**: Sequential memory access patterns for spatial locality

## Code Example
```javascript
class StreamingAnalyticsStore {
  constructor(W, kQueries, mKeys) {
    this.W = W;
    this.blocks = [];
    this.head = 0;
    this.size = 0;
    this.windowSum = 0;
    this.queryRanges = kQueries.map(([start, end]) => ({ start, end }));
    this.keySet = new Set(mKeys);
  }

  appendBatch(newBlocks) {
    for (const block of newBlocks) {
      if (this.size === this.W) {
        this.windowSum -= this.blocks[this.head];
      }
      this.blocks[this.head] = block;
      this.windowSum += block;
      this.head = (this.head + 1) % this.W;
      this.size = Math.min(this.size + 1, this.W);
    }
  }

  rangeSum(queryIndex) {
    const { start, end } = this.queryRanges[queryIndex];
    const windowSize = this.size;
    const startIdx = (this.head - end + this.W) % this.W;
    const endIdx = (this.head - start - 1 + this.W) % this.W;
    let sum = 0;
    let i = startIdx;
    while (i !== (endIdx + 1) % this.W) {
      sum += this.blocks[i];
      i = (i + 1) % this.W;
    }
    return sum;
  }

  hasKey(key) {
    return this.keySet.has(key);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked\n\nTests understanding of streaming frequency estimation under tight memory. The MG approach gives a bounded-memory alternative to exact counts, with concrete guarantees and practical trade-offs in real-time systems.\n\n## Key Concepts\n- Streaming algorithms, Misra-Gries, bounded counters, frequency estimation, error bounds, exact vs. approximate modes.\n- Trade-offs: k vs accuracy, batch size B vs throughput.\n\n## Code Example\n```javascript
class MGMode {
  constructor(k){
    this.k = k;
    this.counters = new Map();
  }
  add(x){
    if (this.counters.has(x)) this.counters.set(x, this.counters.get(x)+1);
    else if (this.counters.size < this.k) this.counters.set(x,1);
    else {
      for (const key of Array.from(this.counters.keys()))
        this.counters.set(key, this.counters.get(key)-1);
      for (const [key,c] of Array.from(this.counters))
        if (c<=0) this.counters.delete(key);
    }
  }
  estimate(){
    let best = null, bestc = -1;
    for (const [k,c] of this.counters) if (c>bestc){ bestc=c; best=k; }
    return best;
  }
}
```

